{"$schema":"https://json.schemastore.org/sarif-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"artifacts":[{"contents":{"text":"<scxml xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml\" version=\"1.0\" datamodel=\"ecmascript\" initial=\"a\">\n  <datamodel><data id=\"d\" expr=\"0\"/></datamodel>\n  <script>function keep(_event) { _event = 1; return _event; }</script>\n  <state id=\"a\">\n    <onentry>\n      <script>delete _event; _name += '!';</script>\n      <script>Reflect.deleteProperty(globalThis, '_event'); delete globalThis._ioprocessors;</script>\n      <assign location=\"d\" expr=\"_sessionid = 'mine'\"/>\n    </onentry>\n    <transition event=\"go\" target=\"f\"/>\n  </state>\n  <final id=\"f\"/>\n</scxml>\n"},"location":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml077-system-variable-writes.scxml"},"mimeType":"application/scxml+xml"}],"columnKind":"utf16CodeUnits","properties":{"diagnosticCounts":{"errors":0,"notes":0,"total":5,"warnings":5},"producer":{"kind":"validator"}},"results":[{"level":"warning","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml077-system-variable-writes.scxml"},"region":{"endColumn":28,"endLine":6,"startColumn":22,"startLine":6}}}],"message":{"markdown":"`<script>` changes the system variable `_event`\n\n**Note:** SCXML 1.0 §5.10: \"The Processor MUST cause any attempt to change the value of a system variable to fail and MUST place the error 'error.execution' on the internal event queue when such an attempt is made.\" The change fails at run time with `error.execution`; a non-strict `delete` or a reflective deletion through the global object returns `false` without one (a known limitation, docs/spec-errata.md). Variable names beginning with '_' are reserved for system use, and '_x' is the root of platform-specific system variables.\n\n**Help:** copy `_event` into a `<data>` variable and change that copy, or use a name that does not begin with `_`\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §5.10 System Variables\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §B.2 The ECMAScript Data Model","text":"`<script>` changes the system variable `_event`"},"properties":{"byteSpan":{"end":276,"start":270},"category":"lint"},"ruleId":"SCXML077"},{"level":"warning","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml077-system-variable-writes.scxml"},"region":{"endColumn":35,"endLine":6,"startColumn":30,"startLine":6}}}],"message":{"markdown":"`<script>` changes the system variable `_name`\n\n**Note:** SCXML 1.0 §5.10: \"The Processor MUST cause any attempt to change the value of a system variable to fail and MUST place the error 'error.execution' on the internal event queue when such an attempt is made.\" The change fails at run time with `error.execution`; a non-strict `delete` or a reflective deletion through the global object returns `false` without one (a known limitation, docs/spec-errata.md). Variable names beginning with '_' are reserved for system use, and '_x' is the root of platform-specific system variables.\n\n**Help:** copy `_name` into a `<data>` variable and change that copy, or use a name that does not begin with `_`\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §5.10 System Variables\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §B.2 The ECMAScript Data Model","text":"`<script>` changes the system variable `_name`"},"properties":{"byteSpan":{"end":283,"start":278},"category":"lint"},"ruleId":"SCXML077"},{"level":"warning","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml077-system-variable-writes.scxml"},"region":{"endColumn":58,"endLine":7,"startColumn":50,"startLine":7}}}],"message":{"markdown":"`<script>` changes the system variable `_event`\n\n**Note:** SCXML 1.0 §5.10: \"The Processor MUST cause any attempt to change the value of a system variable to fail and MUST place the error 'error.execution' on the internal event queue when such an attempt is made.\" The change fails at run time with `error.execution`; a non-strict `delete` or a reflective deletion through the global object returns `false` without one (a known limitation, docs/spec-errata.md). Variable names beginning with '_' are reserved for system use, and '_x' is the root of platform-specific system variables.\n\n**Help:** copy `_event` into a `<data>` variable and change that copy, or use a name that does not begin with `_`\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §5.10 System Variables\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §B.2 The ECMAScript Data Model","text":"`<script>` changes the system variable `_event`"},"properties":{"byteSpan":{"end":358,"start":350},"category":"lint"},"ruleId":"SCXML077"},{"level":"warning","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml077-system-variable-writes.scxml"},"region":{"endColumn":92,"endLine":7,"startColumn":79,"startLine":7}}}],"message":{"markdown":"`<script>` changes the system variable `_ioprocessors`\n\n**Note:** SCXML 1.0 §5.10: \"The Processor MUST cause any attempt to change the value of a system variable to fail and MUST place the error 'error.execution' on the internal event queue when such an attempt is made.\" The change fails at run time with `error.execution`; a non-strict `delete` or a reflective deletion through the global object returns `false` without one (a known limitation, docs/spec-errata.md). Variable names beginning with '_' are reserved for system use, and '_x' is the root of platform-specific system variables.\n\n**Help:** copy `_ioprocessors` into a `<data>` variable and change that copy, or use a name that does not begin with `_`\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §5.10 System Variables\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §B.2 The ECMAScript Data Model","text":"`<script>` changes the system variable `_ioprocessors`"},"properties":{"byteSpan":{"end":392,"start":379},"category":"lint"},"ruleId":"SCXML077"},{"level":"warning","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml077-system-variable-writes.scxml"},"region":{"endColumn":44,"endLine":8,"startColumn":34,"startLine":8}}}],"message":{"markdown":"`expr` on `<assign>` changes the system variable `_sessionid`\n\n**Note:** SCXML 1.0 §5.10: \"The Processor MUST cause any attempt to change the value of a system variable to fail and MUST place the error 'error.execution' on the internal event queue when such an attempt is made.\" The change fails at run time with `error.execution`; a non-strict `delete` or a reflective deletion through the global object returns `false` without one (a known limitation, docs/spec-errata.md). Variable names beginning with '_' are reserved for system use, and '_x' is the root of platform-specific system variables.\n\n**Help:** copy `_sessionid` into a `<data>` variable and change that copy, or use a name that does not begin with `_`\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §5.10 System Variables\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §B.2 The ECMAScript Data Model","text":"`expr` on `<assign>` changes the system variable `_sessionid`"},"properties":{"byteSpan":{"end":446,"start":436},"category":"lint"},"ruleId":"SCXML077"}],"tool":{"driver":{"informationUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/","name":"scxml-validator","rules":[{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"SCXML 1.0 §5.10: \"The Processor MUST cause any attempt to change the value of a system variable to fail and MUST place the error 'error.execution' on the internal event queue when such an attempt is made.\" The document is conformant and the attempt fails at run time with `error.execution`, so this is a warning: the change never happens. The validator reports an assignment, compound assignment, update, or `delete` of `_event`, `_sessionid`, `_name`, `_ioprocessors`, or the platform root `_x`, and the static forms that write one through the global object (`globalThis._event = 1`, `delete globalThis['_event']`, `Reflect.deleteProperty(globalThis, '_event')`, `Reflect.defineProperty`, `Reflect.set`, `Object.defineProperty`), outside a scope that declares the name as its own (a function's variables and parameters, a block's `let`/`const`, a `for` head, a `catch` parameter). A non-strict or reflective deletion currently returns `false` without `error.execution` (a known limitation recorded in docs/spec-errata.md)"},"help":{"text":"How to fix: copy the system variable into a `<data>` variable and change the copy, or use a name that does not begin with `_`.\n\nSpecification: SCXML 1.0 §5.10 System Variables\n\nRun `scxml-cli --explain SCXML077` for examples."},"helpUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/#SystemVariables","id":"SCXML077","name":"SCXML077","properties":{"category":"semantic"},"shortDescription":{"text":"an expression or `<script>` changes a system variable itself"}}],"semanticVersion":"0.2.0"}}}],"version":"2.1.0"}